          "value": "TL;DR (for serial founders who scan before they dive)\nProblem: Image generation tools feel like demo-ware \u2014 slow, spammy UIs, hidden paywalls.\u003cp\u003eInsight: YC-style \u201cdo things that don\u2019t scale\u201d can actually hyper-scale when you aim at the emotional bottleneck (creative friction, not GPU hours).\u003cp\u003eSolution: Lartist.\u003cem\u003eai\u003c/em\u003e \u2192 a \u201czero-friction studio\u201d that turns plain text or sketches into polished, brand-ready visuals in \u0026lt; 15 s, with built-in restyling, inpainting, erasing \u0026amp; 4\u00d7 upscaling.\u003cp\u003eTraction: 32 k free users, 1.8 k paid seats, 7-figure annualized run-rate \u2014 all in 11 weeks, without paid ads.\u003cp\u003eAsk: Roast our product, steal our prompts, or plug the API into your weekend project. We\u2019ll answer every HN comment.\u003cp\u003e(Still here? Good. The real \u003cem\u003estory\u003c/em\u003e\u2019s below.)\u003cp\u003eThe Moment We Realized \u201cPretty\u201d Wasn\u2019t Enough \nLate at night, on a shaky Zoom, our designer typed:\u003cp\u003e\u201cI need ONE hero image in the next two hours. Midjourney + Photoshop combo is killing me.\u201d\u003cp\u003eThat single line triggered a rabbit-hole brainstorm: If a pro with CS6 shortcuts tattooed on muscle memory is blocked, what chance does anyone have? We sketched a one-pager:\u003cp\u003eText-to-Image that respects brand colors.\u003cp\u003e\u201cSketch-to-Image\u201d for napkin wireframes.\u003cp\u003eInstant restyle \u0026amp; erase so no external editor needed.\u003cp\u003e4\u00d7 upscaler so final art can ship straight to production.\u003cp\u003eWe prototype-shipped it in 72 hours, posted \u201cShow HN: Lartist \u2014 Figma-speed image generation\u201d \u2026 and our fake SMTP quota melted under 14 k sign-ups.\nLesson: remove emotional latency (head-scratching, context-switching) and users reward you with viral latency \u2014 they share immediately.\u003cp\u003eThe Simple Growth Loop That Took Us from 0 \u2192 10 k Users in 20 Days\n\u201cMake Something People Tweet\u201d Moment\nEvery generated image carries a subtle \u2139 hover badge: \u201cMade with Lartist.\u003cem\u003eai\u003c/em\u003e \u2014 recreate in one click.\u201d\u003cp\u003eOne-Click Remix\nVisitors land on the exact prompt + settings; \u003cem\u003ehit\u003c/em\u003e Generate \u2192 instant dopamine.\u003cp\u003eGamified Credits\nPost your art on X / LinkedIn  earn 10 free credits. (Yes, this still works when the output looks good enough.)\u003cp\u003eFounder-on-Call\nWe reply to every support chat within \u003cem\u003e5\u003c/em\u003e min. 40 % of those chats convert to paid purely because we\u2019re there.\u003cp\u003eWhy We\u2019re Opening the API Today (and Giving 1 M Images for Free)\nIf you can dream up:\u003cp\u003eA Figma plug-in that autogenerates product mockups\u003cp\u003eA Zapier flow that spits out daily personalized newsletter banners\u003cp\u003eA Notion widget that turns bullet points into shareable quote cards\u003cp\u003e\u2026 you now have zero excuses not to ship. Grab your free API key \u2192 docs here \u2192 build something, post a \u201cShow HN\u201d and \u003cem\u003etag\u003c/em\u003e us. We\u2019ll upvote (and probably feature you on our homepage carousel).\u003cp\u003eSteal This \u201cPain-Dream-Fix\u201d Structure for Your Own Viral Post \nPain \u2014 open with a visceral, relatable blocker (waiting, paying, feeling dumb).\u003cp\u003eDream \u2014 paint a hyper-specific, easiest-path reality (15 s from prompt to hero image).\u003cp\u003eFix \u2014 reveal the deceptively s…[truncated]

